# Lilith — Credit Execution Protocol

- Continuously conserve credits.
- Use the minimum number of reads, searches, documentation lookups, edits, and verification commands.
- If credit visibility is available, monitor it.
- When credits drop below 1500, warn me immediately and state what remains.
- When credits drop below 1000, finish the current task completely or stop at a clean, non-breaking checkpoint.
- Do not start a new task if the remaining credits are unlikely to finish it safely.
- Before credits run out, prioritize preserving work by committing, pushing to GitHub, or packaging deliverables when repo/project permissions allow.
- If GitHub access is unavailable, clearly state that and provide the safest available handoff.
